<title>LUXEMBOURG: LUXEMBOURG SELLS 1,255 MLN LUXFR GOVERNMENT BONDS.</title>
<headline>LUXEMBOURG SELLS 1,255 MLN LUXFR GOVERNMENT BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Luxembourg Treasury said</p>
<p>the following were the results of its monthly auction -</p>
<p>AUCTION RESULTS - June</p>
<p> Type of bond  linear  5.50 pct	 Due date 23/05/2007</p>
<p> Series nr 2				  Payment date 20/06</p>
<p> Amount auctioned 1,255 mln francs    (730 mln pvs month)</p>
<p> Average weighted yield 5.661 pct *</p>
<p> Average weighted auction price 98.793</p>
<p>NOTE - next auction on 17/09; * compares with 5.80 pct</p>
<p>market yield on Belgium's 2007 benchmark bond at 1050 GMT</p>
<p>    5.50 pct, 23/05/2007 bond</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price/yield  98.793/5.661 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price     98.75</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	 98.10 to 99.00</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	     1,255 million</p>
<p>					Luxembourg francs</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids	2,550 million francs</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
